# mutgap3_res_iosfc_compression_type_v2: A descriptor's base compressionType reaches the IOSurface as kIOSurfacePlaneCompressionType (a v1 descriptor's is copied into the v2 form the map works on): v1 and v2, a 16x8 BGRA surface with compressionType 1, 2 and 0, then a one-plane surface (a good plane) with compressionType 1 and 0, each on its own data page, mapped then tested (3); each map's and test's status and each data page after the test are locked. Measured: every map succeeds and every type gives the same test writes as type 0 (IOSurface takes no compression from the surface-level key). The v1 case with type 1 is the process's first map of a nonzero type.
